        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Determination of the Interior Structure of Europa from Gravity and Magnetic Data</title>\n<style>\n  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body { font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.4; color: #000; background: #fff; }\n\n  .header-bar {\n    background: #000;\n    color: #fff;\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    align-items: center;\n    padding: 12px 30px;\n  }\n  .header-bar .agency-name { font-size: 14px; }\n  .header-bar .nasa-logo {\n    width: 60px; height: 60px;\n    background: #000;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n    color: #fff; font-weight: bold; font-size: 18px;\n    border: 2px solid #fff;\n  }\n\n  .title-banner {\n    background: #7cb342;\n    color: #fff;\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: 20px 30px 25px;\n  }\n  .title-banner .subtitle { font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px; }\n  .title-banner h1 { font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 15px; }\n  .title-banner .author { font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 5px; }\n  .title-banner .coauthors { font-size: 18px; }\n\n  .main-content {\n    display: flex;\n    padding: 15px 20px;\n    gap: 20px;\n  }\n  .left-column {\n    flex: 1;\n    min-width: 0;\n  }\n  .right-column {\n    flex: 1;\n    min-width: 0;\n  }\n\n  .section-title {\n    font-size: 16px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    margin-top: 12px;\n    margin-bottom: 4px;\n  }\n  .section-title:first-child { margin-top: 0; }\n\n  .left-column p { margin-bottom: 8px; text-align: justify; }\n  .left-column ol { margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px; }\n  .left-column ol li { margin-bottom: 6px; }\n\n  .figure-container {\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n  }\n  .figure-placeholder {\n    width: 100%;\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n    background: #f5f5f5;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n  .figure-placeholder img {\n    max-width: 100%;\n    height: auto;\n  }\n  .figure-caption {\n    font-size: 11px;\n    margin-top: 5px;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n  }\n\n  .footer {\n    display: flex;\n    padding: 15px 20px;\n    gap: 20px;\n    border-top: 1px solid #ccc;\n    margin-top: 10px;\n  }\n  .footer-left {\n    flex: 1;\n    font-size: 12px;\n  }\n  .footer-left p { margin-bottom: 4px; }\n  .footer-left .bold { font-weight: bold; }\n  .footer-right {\n    flex: 1.5;\n    border: 1px solid #333;\n    padding: 12px 15px;\n    font-size: 12px;\n  }\n  .footer-right .pub-title { font-weight: bold; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 6px; }\n  .footer-right p { margin-bottom: 4px; }\n  .footer-right .contact-title { font-weight: bold; font-size: 14px; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 6px; }\n  .footer-right .contact-info { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; font-size: 14px; }\n  .footer-right .contact-info .email { font-style: italic; }\n\n  .chart-img {\n    width: 100%;\n    height: auto;\n  }\n\n  .histogram-chart {\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 280px;\n    background: #fff;\n    border: 1px solid #999;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  .heatmap-chart {\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 320px;\n    background: #fff;\n    border: 1px solid #999;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n\n  .bold-text { font-weight: bold; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"header-bar\">\n  <div class=\"agency-name\">National Aeronautics and Space Administration</div>\n  <div class=\"nasa-logo\">NASA</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"title-banner\">\n  <div class=\"subtitle\">Postdoc Research</div>\n  <h1>Determination of the Interior Structure of Europa<br>from Gravity and Magnetic Data</h1>\n  <div class=\"author\">Flavio Petricca (JPL Postdoctoral Fellow, 322)</div>\n  <div class=\"coauthors\">J. Castillo-Rogez (4000), S. Vance (322), M. Melwani Daswani (322), C. Cochrane (322)</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"main-content\">\n  <div class=\"left-column\">\n\n    <div class=\"section-title\">Background</div>\n    <p>The Galileo mission provided measurements of <span class=\"bold-text\">Europa's gravity and magnetic fields</span>, indicating that the moon hosts a subsurface ocean and that its interior is mostly made by rocks (90 wt. %). However, the interior structure is still poorly understood, with <span class=\"bold-text\">the main uncertainties affecting the ice shell thickness and ocean depth, and the size of a putative metallic core</span> whose existence was inferred from the first analysis of Galileo's gravity data (Anderson et al., 1998). A recent reanalysis indicated a smaller level of differentiation (Gomez-Casajus et al., 2021), challenging the inference of the existence of the metallic core. Knowledge of the degree of differentiation is crucial to understand the origins and evolution of Europa. Furthermore, <span class=\"bold-text\">gravity and magnetic data</span> have only been used separately, and developing methodologies to <span class=\"bold-text\">jointly analyze</span> them will be fundamental for <span class=\"bold-text\">Europa Clipper's investigations</span>.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"section-title\">Objectives</div>\n    <p>We analyze measurements of Europa's gravity and magnetic fields based on Galileo data with <span class=\"bold-text\">new generation interior models and techniques</span> to answer the following questions:</p>\n    <ol>\n      <li>Did Europa differentiate a metallic core? What is the composition of the rocky mantle?</li>\n      <li>How can we combine gravity and magnetic data in an effective way to infer the ice thickness and ocean depth and salinity?</li>\n    </ol>\n\n    <div class=\"section-title\">Approach and Results</div>\n    <p>We developed new interior models that use Bayesian inference and Markov-chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithms to combine gravity and magnetic observations with geochemical data on the composition of the ocean and the rocky mantle. Our two main results are:</p>\n    <ol>\n      <li>Our models indicate that Europa <span class=\"bold-text\">did not differentiate a metallic core (Figure 1)</span>. This implies that <span class=\"bold-text\">Europa's evolution was colder</span> than previously thought. The resulting structure and composition of the rocky mantle indicates that <span class=\"bold-text\">Europa and the Jupiter system likely formed from dry CV chondrite-like material</span>.</li>\n      <li>The combination of gravity and magnetic data can <span class=\"bold-text\">separately constrain the ice shell and ocean thicknesses</span>, while separate inversions are degenerate <span class=\"bold-text\">(Figure 2)</span>.</li>\n    </ol>\n\n    <div class=\"section-title\">Significance of Results/Benefits to NASA/JPL</div>\n    <p>The unprecedented constraint on the structure of the deep interior <span class=\"bold-text\">changes our understanding of the evolution of Europa</span>. The lack of a metallic core indicates a cold evolution, with implications for the origin of the Jupiter system and the evolution of the other Galilean moons. The <span class=\"bold-text\">methodology developed to combine gravity and magnetic data will be fundamental in the context of Europa Clipper's interior science</span>. This technique will provide a framework to connect interior models with the results of ongoing lab work at JPL (PSIE, PI: S. Vance). New experimental data on the thermodynamic and electric properties of solutions relevant to Europa's ocean are being collected and will be implemented in this interior modeling framework.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"section-title\">Future Work</div>\n    <p>The framework developed will be expanded to include new experimental data in preparation for the analysis of Europa Clipper's data. It will be also applied to Ganymede, Callisto and Titan to explore their interiors. Finally, ongoing work includes the application of this framework to the moons of Uranus in the context of the formulation of the Uranus Orbiter and Probe, highly prioritized by the Planetary Science Decadal Survey.</p>\n\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"right-column\">\n\n    <div class=\"figure-container\">\n      <div class=\"figure-placeholder\" style=\"height: 290px;\">\n        <svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 280\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n          <!-- Panel A -->\n          <rect x=\"10\" y=\"5\" width=\"480\" height=\"130\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#999\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/>\n          <text x=\"18\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">a</text>\n          <!-- Y axis labels -->\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">10000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">8000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">6000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">4000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">2000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">0</text>\n          <!-- Y axis label -->\n          <text x=\"2\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" transform=\"rotate(-90, 2, 80)\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Samples</text>\n          <!-- Grid lines -->\n          <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/>\n          <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/>\n          <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"75\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"75\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/>\n          <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/>\n          <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"125\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"125\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/>\n          <!-- Histogram shape - Panel A: peak around 400-450 -->\n          <path d=\"M40,130 L60,128 L80,125 L100,122 L120,118 L140,112 L160,105 L180,95 L200,82 L220,68 L240,52 L260,38 L280,28 L300,22 L320,18 L340,16 L360,15 L380,16 L400,20 L420,28 L440,42 L460,65 L480,100 L490,125 L490,130 Z\" fill=\"#8899cc\" opacity=\"0.7\"/>\n          <path d=\"M40,130 L60,128 L80,125 L100,122 L120,118 L140,112 L160,105 L180,95 L200,82 L220,68 L240,52 L260,38 L280,28 L300,22 L320,18 L340,16 L360,15 L380,16 L400,20 L420,28 L440,42 L460,65 L480,100 L490,125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4466aa\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n          <!-- Dashed lines -->\n          <line x1=\"290\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/>\n          <line x1=\"400\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/>\n          <!-- X axis -->\n          <text x=\"40\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"7\">0</text>\n          <text x=\"130\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"7\">100</text>\n          <text x=\"220\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"7\">200</text>\n          <text x=\"310\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"7\">300</text>\n          <text x=\"400\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"7\">400</text>\n          <text x=\"490\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"7\">500</text>\n          <text x=\"265\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Core Radius [km]</text>\n\n          <!-- Panel B -->\n          <rect x=\"10\" y=\"155\" width=\"480\" height=\"120\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#999\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/>\n          <text x=\"18\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">b</text>\n          <!-- Y axis labels -->\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">6000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">5000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">4000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">3000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"end\">2000</text>\n          <text x=\"5\" y=\"275\" font-si